Z||000000||Shaun41178||04-28-2001||10:07 PM||||Didn't feel like trying to find the post where this was asked but I know some of you have been wondering what happened to NRT.  Well the owners I guess decided to split up or something.  Don't really know but not my business anyways.  <P>Anyways NRT is now Nu-tek and is owned by Nick Norris.  The same guy that does the head and cam packages for the 60 degree v6 engines.  Here is the website for Nu-tek.<BR> <A HREF="http://site.quickbooks.com/sites/57/31/0a/nutekmotorsports45840/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://site.quickbooks.com/sites/57/31/0a/nutekmotorsports45840/index.html</A> <P>Hope this helps.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
